WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.213
Say you earn twenty pounds from chores this month and spend fifteen. Twenty minus fifteen: you are five pounds ahead. Countries do the same sum with their trade.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:24.886
Exports bring money in. Imports send money out. Trade in goods is visible. Trade in services is invisible.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:41.650
So there are three balances. Visible balance: exports of goods minus imports of goods. Invisible balance: exports of services minus imports of services. Add the two to get the current account balance.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:48.265
Read the sign. A positive balance is a surplus. A negative balance is a deficit.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:01:02.195
Step one. Choose the right rows. Visible means goods only. Invisible means services only. The current account uses them all.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:14.338
Step two. Write exports minus imports. Step three. Keep the sign. Step four. Give the currency and units.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:30.907
Here is a real question from June 2025. Figure one shows a country's exports and imports in billions of euros. Calculate the visible trade balance. Two marks.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:44.844
Visible means goods, so use only the goods rows. Exports of goods are one hundred and fifty billion. Imports of goods are one hundred and twenty billion. Ignore the services rows.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:50.095
Goods exports are bigger than goods imports, so we expect a surplus.

00:01:50.680 --> 00:02:01.731
One hundred and fifty minus one hundred and twenty is thirty. The visible trade balance is thirty billion euros, a surplus. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:14.436
A common mistake is using every row when the question asks for visible trade. That gives forty billion, which is the current account, not the visible balance.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:23.126
Another is subtracting the wrong way. Imports minus exports flips the sign and turns a surplus into a deficit.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:43.285
Now you try, with example figures in billions of dollars. Exports of goods sixty, exports of services twenty-five, imports of goods seventy-five, imports of services fifteen. Calculate the visible balance and the current account balance. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:54.801
A: goods only. Sixty minus seventy-five is minus fifteen. The visible balance is minus fifteen billion dollars, a deficit.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:03:08.764
B: services are twenty-five minus fifteen, which is plus ten. Add the visible balance: minus fifteen plus ten is minus five. The current account is minus five billion dollars, a deficit.

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:18.824
The check agrees. Total exports are eighty-five billion, total imports ninety billion. Imports are bigger, so it is a deficit.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:27.170
Remember: choose the right rows, subtract exports minus imports, keep the sign, and give the units. Now try the practice questions.
